      "sourceHash": "bce217531c743629a0ad5219303f9656603eaa3f366a02980cd1f95c688b2926",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 2.13,
          "en": "And you'll be greeted with an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 6.9,
          "en": "because previously, when I used the built-in img element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.9,
          "end": 9.18,
          "en": "instead of the next image element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.18,
          "end": 14.18,
          "en": "I set the source by accessing the imported thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.69,
          "end": 19.59,
          "en": "So the thing that's actually stored in this logo variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.59,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "in this file here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 23.61,
          "en": "and by then accessing the source property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.61,
          "end": 26.16,
          "en": "on that imported thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.16,
          "end": 29.85,
          "en": "So that logo thing I'm importing here seems to be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.85,
          "end": 32.04,
          "en": "that has a src property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.04,
          "end": 35.73,
          "en": "and I'm using the value stored in that src property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.73,
          "end": 38.61,
          "en": "as a value for the src prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.61,
          "end": 42.693,
          "en": "at least that is what worked when I used the built-in image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "Now, with the next image being used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 48.33,
          "en": "that needs to change though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.33,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "You now need to set the entire logo object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 55.38,
          "en": "that describes this image file to which we're linking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.38,
          "end": 57.063,
          "en": "as a value for src.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.08,
          "end": 60.96,
          "en": "So you no longer access the src property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.96,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "but you set the entire logo image object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 66.633,
          "en": "as a value for the src prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "And if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "and save everything, you'll notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 75.033,
          "en": "that everything works again and the error is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.87,
          "end": 79.02,
          "en": "Now, why do we need to make this change though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.02,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "Well, we need to make this change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 86.1,
          "en": "because this logo thing here is actually not a path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.1,
          "end": 88.62,
          "en": "to the image or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.62,
          "end": 92.19,
          "en": "Instead, we can console.log logo here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.19,
          "end": 95.37,
          "en": "to look into it and see what's stored in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.37,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "and what exactly gets generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 100.113,
          "en": "by Next.js when we add this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.4,
          "end": 103.41,
          "en": "And what we'll see is that we'll have an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.41,
          "end": 105.75,
          "en": "that looks something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "which includes some path to the image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "It's not the actual path to this logo PNG file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 116.13,
          "en": "but instead a path that will work after deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "or also already during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 120.36,
          "en": "But in the end, it's a path to the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.36,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "that has already been processed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 126.69,
          "en": "by the Next.js build process or development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.69,
          "end": 129.45,
          "en": "and that has been copied into a different location,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.45,
          "end": 131.97,
          "en": "as you can tell, but it's not just that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.97,
          "end": 133.77,
          "en": "Instead, this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.77,
          "end": 136.62,
          "en": "that's generated when we import the image here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.62,
          "end": 139.825,
          "en": "actually also contains height and width information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.825,
          "end": 141.96,
          "en": "about the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.96,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "and that's important for this image component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.74,
          "end": 149.4,
          "en": "as you can also learn in this image component documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.4,
          "end": 152.223,
          "en": "in the official Next.js docs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.3,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "because this height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 158.07,
          "en": "and width information is needed by Next.js to determine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.07,
          "end": 160.89,
          "en": "how exactly that image should be displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.89,
          "end": 162.29,
          "en": "and how it should be loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.44,
          "end": 167.79,
          "en": "Because if we now inspect that image on the rendered page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.79,
          "end": 170.85,
          "en": "you will see that this Next.js image component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.85,
          "end": 173.7,
          "en": "does in the end still render the standard image element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.7,
          "end": 176.79,
          "en": "but it renders this image element with a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 178.54,
          "en": "of settings on it, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.55,
          "end": 181.8,
          "en": "For example, it sets loading to lazy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.8,
          "end": 184.11,
          "en": "which makes sure that the image is only loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.11,
          "end": 187.08,
          "en": "and displayed if it's actually visible on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.08,
          "end": 189.99,
          "en": "That's a mechanism built into the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.99,
          "end": 192.66,
          "en": "but it, for example, also sets the width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.66,
          "end": 195.48,
          "en": "and that's the width and height as it was determined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.48,
          "end": 198.09,
          "en": "from that file we were importing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.09,
          "end": 199.59,
          "en": "And this width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.59,
          "end": 203.34,
          "en": "and height information is required by Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.34,
          "end": 207.39,
          "en": "to avoid layout shift where the layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.39,
          "end": 209.79,
          "en": "and the elements on the screen jump around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.79,
          "end": 212.04,
          "en": "after an image is loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.04,
          "end": 213.42000000000002,
          "en": "By setting this width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213.42000000000002,
          "end": 216.12,
          "en": "and height here, NextJS makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.12,
          "end": 219.66,
          "en": "that the appropriate space for that image is reserved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.66,
          "end": 222.81,
          "en": "so that it doesn't suddenly move elements around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.81,
          "end": 224.28300000000002,
          "en": "as it's being displayed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.69,
          "end": 227.49,
          "en": "In addition, this width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.49,
          "end": 229.47,
          "en": "and height information also helps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 232.77,
          "en": "with serving different image files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.77,
          "end": 237.66,
          "en": "with different sizes for different screen densities.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.66,
          "end": 241.14,
          "en": "That's something Next.js does out of the box here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.14,
          "end": 245.76,
          "en": "and that's what this srcset attribute here is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.76,
          "end": 249.66,
          "en": "This was also added automatically by Next.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249.66,
          "end": 252.93,
          "en": "and this srcset attribute in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 252.93,
          "end": 256.38,
          "en": "tells the browser to load different images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.38,
          "end": 259.743,
          "en": "for different screen resolution densities.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 264.36,
          "en": "And you can see that this srcset attribute points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.36,
          "end": 269.19,
          "en": "at different image URLs, which are almost exactly the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.19,
          "end": 272.7,
          "en": "but which have this different query parameter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.7,
          "end": 277.7,
          "en": "inside of it where some width is set in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.01,
          "end": 282.15,
          "en": "and images with those widths are in the end generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 282.15,
          "end": 286.14,
          "en": "dynamically, you could say, by Next.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 286.14,
          "end": 289.77,
          "en": "as the image is served on different screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 289.77,
          "end": 292.83,
          "en": "of different resolutions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.83,
          "end": 295.23,
          "en": "So the Next.js image component renders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 295.23,
          "end": 298.2,
          "en": "such a native image element, and as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.2,
          "end": 300.63,
          "en": "this width and height setting here is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 300.63,
          "end": 302.61,
          "en": "to know for Next.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.61,
          "end": 305.31,
          "en": "but that is determined automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 305.31,
          "end": 307.17,
          "en": "when you're importing a file locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.17,
          "end": 310.44,
          "en": "However, you can override the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.44,
          "end": 313.263,
          "en": "and height that's assumed by Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
